{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LQttmaUkMZKbpfujL9Gx3Y","type":"tool_result","content":"mesh || MUT: optional repository-local control plane; run/cancel/resume/accept/finish/setup mutate disposable mesh state while canonical acceptance still calls Task-Spec\n    Usage: taskspec mesh <init|doctor|serve|frontier|run|status|watch|explain|cancel|resume|accept|finish|adapters|setup|mcp> ... | taskspec mesh run --initiative <id> [--execute]\ngraph || MUT: none; TaskGraphView/v1 is derived from Markdown and Git\n    Usage: taskspec graph [--task <id>] [--check] [--mermaid] [--json] | taskspec graph --initiative <id> --view tasks|capabilities\nstatus || MUT: none; emits TaskStatus/v1 and exactly one safe next command\n    Usage: taskspec status <task-id-or-path> [--json] | taskspec status --initiative <id>\nmesh init || MUT: mutates TaskMesh state; never grants a TaskSpec seal\n    Usage: taskspec mesh init \nmesh doctor || MUT: may initialize a missing daemon and write Git metadata; does not seal or accept tasks\n    Usage: taskspec mesh doctor \nmesh serve || MUT: mutates TaskMesh state; never grants a TaskSpec seal\n    Usage: taskspec mesh serve --foreground\nmesh frontier || MUT: may initialize a missing daemon and write Git metadata; does not seal or accept tasks\n    Usage: taskspec mesh frontier \nmesh run || MUT: mutates TaskMesh state; never grants a TaskSpec seal\n    Usage: taskspec mesh run --task <id>|--frontier|--initiative <id> [--adapter <name>] [--model <id>] [--provider <id>] [--mode supervised|autonomous] [--max-parallel <n>] [--execute]\nmesh status || MUT: uninitialized status is read-only; existing runtime inspection may restart its daemon\n    Usage: taskspec mesh status [<run-or-attempt>]\nmesh watch || MUT: may initialize a missing daemon and write Git metadata; does not seal or accept tasks\n    Usage: taskspec mesh watch <run> [--after <sequence>]\nmesh explain || MUT: may initialize a missing daemon and